---
// Text badges instead of the AWT and AL logos until logo use is approved (PROJECT_CONTEXT §2).
// "A network of labs and plants" replaces the prototype's "dozens": AL has 6 labs and 9 sites
// (Ryan, Oct 14, 2026).
---

<section class="section members" id="memberships">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Memberships</p>
      <h2>Backed by two industry networks.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Power Engineering belongs to the Association of Water Technologies and Associated Labs. Both
        connect our team to training, technical research and peers who solve the same problems every
        day, and that knowledge goes straight into your program.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mem-grid">
      <article class="mem">
        <div class="mem-id">
          <div class="mem-badge" aria-hidden="true">
            AWT
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Association of Water Technologies</h3>
            <span>Member company</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          AWT is the international association for water treatment companies that serve industrial
          and commercial cooling and heating systems. It sets the bar for training and professional
          certification in our industry.
        </p>
        <div class="mem-stats">
          <div>
            <b>500+</b>
            <span>Member companies</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <b>CWT</b>
            <span>Certified Water Technologist credential</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <b>Intl.</b>
            <span>Industry association</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h4>What it means for you</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Technicians trained through AWT technical seminars, webinars and safety courses</li>
          <li>
            A path to the Certified Water Technologist (CWT) credential, which requires five years
            of field experience and a proctored exam
          </li>
          <li>
            Current technical papers and AWT's industry publication, <em>The Analyst</em>
          </li>
          <li>Legionella guidance and water management resources from the association</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="ext" href="https://awt.org/" rel="noopener">
          awt.org &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="mem">
        <div class="mem-id">
          <div class="mem-badge al" aria-hidden="true">
            AL
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Associated Labs</h3>
            <span>Member company</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          Associated Labs is an alliance of privately held, independent water treatment companies,
          each owner-operated. Members work in different regional markets, so they share technical
          knowledge, case studies and best practices openly.
        </p>
        <div class="mem-stats">
          <div>
            <b>9</b>
            <span>Member companies</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <b>9</b>
            <span>Manufacturing and distribution sites</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <b>6</b>
            <span>Labs and R&amp;D facilities</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h4>What it means for you</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Collective expertise across boiler, cooling, closed loop, wastewater and potable
            treatment
          </li>
          <li>
            Shared case work on high-silica towers, data center cooling, tagged polymer monitoring
            and Legionella control
          </li>
          <li>
            Formulation testing on corrosion, scale loops and pilot towers across the member network
          </li>
          <li>
            Support for customers with sites outside Utah and Idaho through shared products and
            services
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a class="ext" href="https://associatedlabs.org/" rel="noopener">
          associatedlabs.org &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mem-band">
      <div>
        <h3>Independent, with national reach.</h3>
        <p>
          Private equity is consolidating the water treatment industry. Power Engineering remains
          privately held and locally run, so decisions about your program are made in Salt Lake City
          by people who know your site.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Someone has already solved it.</h3>
        <p>
          When a system behaves in an unusual way, our team can draw on peers across two countries
          and a network of labs and plants. You get a local team with the knowledge base of a much
          larger organization.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .members {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .mem-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .mem {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 30px 28px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    align-content: start;
    background: var(--bg);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .mem-id {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .mem-badge {
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 6px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-family: var(--f-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--on-brand);
    background: var(--brand);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .mem-badge.al {
    background: var(--deep-2);
    color: var(--deep-ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--deep-line);
  }
  .mem-id h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .mem-id span {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .mem > p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .mem-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .mem-stats div {
    padding: 14px 12px 14px 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .mem-stats b {
    font-family: var(--f-display);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .mem-stats span {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .mem h4 {
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  .mem ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .mem li {
    padding-left: 18px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .mem li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.72em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 1.5px;
    background: var(--brand);
  }
  .ext {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--brand);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .ext:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .mem-band {
    margin-top: 24px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 26px 28px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--deep);
    color: var(--deep-ink);
  }
  .mem-band h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .mem-band p {
    color: var(--deep-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .mem-grid,
    .mem-band {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .mem-stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
